    {
      "id": "p0084-b006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Boku is an informal, masculine Japanese pronoun for “I/me”. Boku carries a sense of boyish-ness, gentleness, timidness, decency, and/or being spoiled, among other things. Other fictional characters who use boku include:",
        "raw": "Baku is an informal, masculine Japanese pronoun for \"I/me\". Baku carries a\nsense of boyish-ness, gentleness, timidness, decency, and/or being spoiled,\namong other things. Other fictional characters who use boku include:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.32085254,
          0.45137857,
